WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.177
A sorted table is much easier to read and check.

2
00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:08.904
In this lesson, you will learn to sort your rows with arrange, from A

3
00:00:08.904 --> 00:00:11.268
to Z, and from Z to A.

4
00:00:11.268 --> 00:00:13.294
It only takes one short line.

5
00:00:13.294 --> 00:00:15.320
Let's put our data in order.

6
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.400
Here is our table, with the new short column names.

7
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.560
Right now, the rows are in the order they came from the survey.

8
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.253
I write a note:

9
00:00:43.253 --> 00:00:46.746
arranging rows, we can ascend or descend the rows.

10
00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:50.627
Ascend means from small to big, or A to Z.

11
00:00:50.627 --> 00:00:52.180
Descend means the opposite.

12
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:07.460
Demographic, pipe, arrange, and inside the brackets, the column to sort by: Province.

13
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:27.538
Run it.

14
00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:30.469
Now the provinces are in alphabetical order:

15
00:01:30.469 --> 00:01:33.400
Badakhshan first, then Farah, and so on.

16
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.318
Next, arrange by Gender.

17
00:01:43.318 --> 00:01:45.745
Run it, and open the table.

18
00:01:45.745 --> 00:01:50.600
Female rows come first, because F comes before M in the alphabet.

19
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:12.800
To reverse the order, wrap the column in desc, short for descending. Arrange, desc, Gender.

20
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.640
Run it, and now Male comes first.

21
00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.740
The same works for numbers:

22
00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.520
arrange household size, and the smallest families come first.

23
00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.040
With desc, the largest come first.

24
00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.624
Arrange, and desc for reverse.

25
00:03:03.624 --> 00:03:08.240
Simple, and very useful when you check your data. Great job today!

